diff --git a/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/README.md b/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aad52fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+# k3s overlay — single VPS
+
+Runs the whole platform on one VPS: k3s, the F5 NGINX Ingress Controller on ports 80/443, and
+cert-manager issuing a Let's Encrypt certificate for your domain.
+
+```text
+Internet ──► :80/:443 (k3s ServiceLB)
+               │
+               ▼
+     NGINX Ingress Controller ── TLS (cert-manager / Let's Encrypt)
+               │
+     platform-gateway Ingress
+               ├── /api/v1/*, /fhir ──► Spring Boot services
+               ├── /graphql          ──► graphql-gateway
+               └── /                 ──► frontend (nginx, SPA)
+                                           │
+                       Postgres · Redis · Kafka · RabbitMQ · MinIO (in-cluster)
+```
+
+**Why not ingress-nginx?** The community `kubernetes/ingress-nginx` project was retired in
+March 2026 and no longer receives security fixes. This overlay uses NGINX's own controller
+(`nginx/kubernetes-ingress`), which reads the same `Ingress` resources. Its annotations are
+`nginx.org/*`, not `nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/*`.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 VPS, **4 vCPU / 8 GB RAM / 40 GB disk** minimum. Images are built on the
+  box, and the Maven build cache takes several GB.
+- A DNS **A record** for your domain pointing at the VPS. With no domain, `<VPS-IP>.sslip.io`
+  works.
+- Nothing else listening on ports 80/443. Remove any host nginx/apache first.
+- Docker, used only to build images: `curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh`
+
+Firewall (if using ufw). Don't expose 6443 publicly:
+
+```bash
+ufw allow 22/tcp && ufw allow 80/tcp && ufw allow 443/tcp
+ufw allow from 10.42.0.0/16 to any   # k3s pods
+ufw allow from 10.43.0.0/16 to any   # k3s services
+ufw enable
+```
+
+## Deploy
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/ayia-hosni/healthcare-microservices-platform.git
+cd healthcare-microservices-platform
+sudo DOMAIN=health.example.com ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com ./infra/k8s/scripts/deploy-to-k3s.sh
+```
+
+The script installs k3s with Traefik disabled, then installs the NGINX Ingress Controller and
+cert-manager through k3s's built-in Helm controller (`platform/`). It generates `secrets.env`
+with random passwords, builds all 11 images, imports them into k3s, and applies this overlay.
+
+The first run takes 20–30 minutes, mostly Maven. Use `ACME_STAGING=1` on the first run if
+you're still testing DNS, so you don't hit Let's Encrypt rate limits.
+
+**Back up `secrets.env`.** Postgres creates its roles with those passwords on first boot.
+Losing the file means losing database access.
+
+## Redeploy
+
+```bash
+git pull
+sudo DOMAIN=health.example.com ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com ./infra/k8s/scripts/deploy-to-k3s.sh
+```
+
+Images are tagged with the git SHA, so only changed services roll. Uncommitted changes get a
+`-dirty-<timestamp>` tag.
+
+### Building on another machine
+
+Use this if the VPS is too small to build while running. Check out the same commit on both
+sides:
+
+```bash
+# local — add --platform linux/amd64 to each build if you're on Apple Silicon
+TAG=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)
+for s in identity-service patient-service doctor-service appointment-service emr-service \
+         billing-service notification-service audit-service analytics-service graphql-gateway; do
+  docker build -t healthcare-platform/$s:$TAG -f backend/$s/Dockerfile backend
+done
+docker build -t healthcare-platform/frontend:$TAG frontend
+docker save $(docker images --format '{{.Repository}}:{{.Tag}}' | grep "^healthcare-platform/.*:$TAG$") \
+  | ssh root@VPS 'cat > /tmp/hp.tar && k3s ctr images import /tmp/hp.tar && rm /tmp/hp.tar'
+
+# VPS
+sudo SKIP_BUILD=1 IMAGE_TAG=<TAG> DOMAIN=... ACME_EMAIL=... ./infra/k8s/scripts/deploy-to-k3s.sh
+```
+
+## Operations
+
+```bash
+export KUBECONFIG=/etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml
+kubectl -n healthcare-platform get pods
+kubectl -n healthcare-platform logs deploy/appointment-service -f
+kubectl -n healthcare-platform describe certificate platform-tls     # TLS issuance status
+kubectl -n nginx-ingress logs deploy/nginx-ingress-controller        # routing / 404s
+```
+
+Switching from staging to a real certificate:
+
+```bash
+kubectl -n healthcare-platform delete certificate platform-tls
+kubectl -n healthcare-platform delete secret platform-tls
+# re-run the deploy script without ACME_STAGING
+```
+
+After editing `secrets.env`, re-run the script, then
+`kubectl -n healthcare-platform rollout restart deployment`. Pods don't pick up Secret changes
+on their own.
+
+## What this overlay changes vs. dev
+
+| | dev (Minikube) | k3s (VPS) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Ingress controller | community ingress-nginx addon | F5 NGINX Ingress Controller |
+| TLS | none | Let's Encrypt via cert-manager |
+| Ingress host | catch-all | your `DOMAIN` |
+| Secrets | dev values committed in Git | generated on the VPS, gitignored |
+| Postgres / MinIO creds | hardcoded | from `platform-secrets` |
+| MinIO storage | ephemeral | 10Gi PVC |
+| Postgres storage | 1Gi PVC | 10Gi PVC |
+| Image tags | `:latest` | git SHA |
+
+Shared with dev: PLAINTEXT Kafka, in-memory Quartz, payer-mock, one replica per workload.
+
+## Not covered
+
+- **Backups.** The PVCs live under `/var/lib/rancher/k3s/storage` on the VPS disk. Schedule
+  `pg_dumpall` (via `kubectl exec`) and copy the MinIO bucket off the box.
+- **Kafka, Redis and RabbitMQ are not persistent.** A pod restart drops in-flight
+  messages. Domain events stay safe in each service's outbox table until relayed.
+- **Real patient data.** A single VPS with self-hosted datastores is not a HIPAA-ready
+  setup. Treat it as a demo environment.
diff --git a/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/datastores/kafka.yaml b/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/datastores/kafka.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8b9c9c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/datastores/kafka.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Dev-only, deliberately simplified. docker-compose's Kafka runs SASL_SSL with a throwaway
+# dev CA (see infra/docker/kafka/) — replicating that cert/JAAS machinery in-cluster is a lot
+# of moving parts for a local dev cluster, so this broker is plain PLAINTEXT instead. The
+# app-side security.protocol override that pairs with this lives in
+# ../patches/kafka-plaintext.yaml.
+apiVersion: apps/v1
+kind: Deployment
+metadata:
+  name: kafka
+  namespace: healthcare-platform
+  labels:
+    app: kafka
+spec:
+  replicas: 1
+  selector:
+    matchLabels:
+      app: kafka
+  template:
+    metadata:
+      labels:
+        app: kafka
+    spec:
+      # Kubernetes auto-injects a KAFKA_PORT=tcp://<clusterIP>:9092 env var into every pod in
+      # this namespace once a Service named "kafka" exists (the legacy Docker-links-style
+      # "service link" behavior). cp-kafka's entrypoint treats KAFKA_PORT as the deprecated
+      # `port` config knob and tries to parse that URL as a bare port number, crashing
+      # instantly. This turns off that env var injection for this pod.
+      enableServiceLinks: false
+      containers:
+        - name: kafka
+          image: confluentinc/cp-kafka:7.6.0
+          ports:
+            - containerPort: 9092
+          env:
+            - name: KAFKA_BROKER_ID
+              value: "1"
+            - name: KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT
+              value: "zookeeper.healthcare-platform.svc.cluster.local:2181"
+            - name: KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS
+              value: "PLAINTEXT://kafka.healthcare-platform.svc.cluster.local:9092"
+            - name: KAFKA_LISTENER_SECURITY_PROTOCOL_MAP
+              value: "PLAINTEXT:PLAINTEXT"
+            - name: KAFKA_OFFSETS_TOPIC_REPLICATION_FACTOR
+              value: "1"
+          resources:
+            requests:
+              cpu: "150m"
+              memory: "384Mi"
+            limits:
+              cpu: "1000m"
+              memory: "768Mi"
+---
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: Service
+metadata:
+  name: kafka
+  namespace: healthcare-platform
+spec:
+  selector:
+    app: kafka
+  ports:
+    - port: 9092
+      targetPort: 9092
+  type: ClusterIP
diff --git a/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/datastores/minio.yaml b/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/datastores/minio.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..24bd8e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/infra/k8s/overlays/k3s/datastores/minio.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Single-node k3s MinIO for emr-service's clinical document attachments. Unlike the dev
+# overlay, root credentials come from platform-secrets (emr-service gets the same values via
+# patches/emr-minio-auth.yaml) and data lives on a PVC so uploads survive restarts.
+# ClusterIP only — never exposed through the Ingress.
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
+metadata:
+  name: minio-data
+  namespace: healthcare-platform
+spec:
+  accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
+  resources:
+    requests:
+      storage: 10Gi
+---
+apiVersion: apps/v1
+kind: Deployment
+metadata:
+  name: minio
+  namespace: healthcare-platform
+  labels:
+    app: minio
+spec:
+  replicas: 1
+  strategy:
+    type: Recreate
+  selector:
+    matchLabels:
+      app: minio
+  template:
+    metadata:
+      labels:
+        app: minio
+    spec:
+      enableServiceLinks: false
+      containers:
+        - name: minio
+          image: minio/minio:latest
+          imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
+          args: ["server", "/data", "--console-address", ":9001"]
+          ports:
+            - containerPort: 9000
+            - containerPort: 9001
+          env:
+            - name: MINIO_ROOT_USER
+              valueFrom:
+                secretKeyRef:
+                  name: platform-secrets
+                  key: MINIO_ROOT_USER
+            - name: MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD
+              valueFrom:
+                secretKeyRef:
+                  name: platform-secrets
+                  key: MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD
+          volumeMounts:
+            - name: data
+              mountPath: /data
+          readinessProbe:
+            httpGet:
+              path: /minio/health/ready
+              port: 9000
+            initialDelaySeconds: 5
+            periodSeconds: 10
+          resources:
+            requests:
+              cpu: "50m"
+              memory: "160Mi"
+            limits:
+              cpu: "500m"
+              memory: "512Mi"
+      volumes:
+        - name: data
+          persistentVolumeClaim:
+            claimName: minio-data
+---
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: Service
+metadata:
+  name: minio
+  namespace: healthcare-platform
+spec:
+  selector:
+    app: minio
+  ports:
+    - name: api
+      port: 9000
+      targetPort: 9000
+    - name: console
+      port: 9001
+      targetPort: 9001
+  type: ClusterIP
